several weeks ago a video showing yiga  blade master  straight up stealing the master sword  took the breath of the wild community by  storm  while it's generally explained that you  just have to bring the yiga blade  masters to the korok forest  to get them to steal the sword exactly  how does this happen  here is why they steal the master sword  and how they do it step by step  and some troubleshooting during the  process if you want more videos  explaining how new breath of the wild  discoveries work  in depth let us know by liking this  video  first found by a twitter user by the  name of bot w back in january 2021  the execution of this trick since then  has become more streamlined after its  initial find  first you'll need to access the yiga  hideout while the yiga are still present  if you have defeated koga the hideout  will be empty and the blade masters will  start spawning in the overworld so you  can't do this trick if koga is defeated  this hideout also won't be active  until you start the divine beast von  nabors quest so you need to have talk to  riju in gerudo town first  now that the yiga are active we head to  the hideout with the goal of drawing the  yiga outside with you  but instead of going in through the  front door of the hideout we instead go  through the rear door  there are two ways to get the yiga's  attention through the back door  one is by shield clipping through the  wall by shield jumping onto this wall to  get skew  then forward shield jumping onto this  wall and unequipping your shield  mid-jump  this will force link straight through  the wall then simply go around to the  right here and fire an arrow at any yiga  member  after they are alerted head back and  climb up the left side of the secret  door  and you're out i recommend killing off  the foot soldiers and most of the blade  masters as you don't really need all of  them  then start climbing and walking towards  a korok forest  you'll want to keep in mind is that how  blade masters work is that they will  teleport to you when you change  elevation and they can't make a straight  walking path to you  otherwise they will continue to walk  very very slowly towards you  so before you walk the entire way to the  korok forest this way which is agonizing  i'm going to suggest using a different  method the better method is first  acquiring the moon jump glitch  by going to the mounted archery mini  game then mounting a wild horse and  staying on it until the timer ends  you'll acquire moon jump  so get the glitch first then teleport to  the tower or use a travel medallion here  if you don't want to walk  all the way to the door when you arrive  jump  throw and switch weapons to get rid of  the grounded slide glitch  then do the alternate method of getting  the ego's attention by whistling here  with your camera turned this way  the blade master will then walk to the  door to search for the noise  use a korok leaf through the wall and  this will alert the others  the difference with this method is it's  taking advantage of the teleportation  trigger by moon jumping five or six  times then falling back down  they'll have thanked you moved on to a  new platform triggering them to teleport  to you  which is much faster than the previous  method you can even loop this several  times  just by jumping a couple times as a  teleport to you now it's still a long  journey but instead of  two hours it's now maybe about 30 to 45  minutes of walking  take this path shown here to the master  [Music]  sword  [Music]  [Music]  a couple tips as you're traveling you'll  want to keep majora's mask on to reduce  random encounters and you'll want some  decent weapons to keep annoying baddies  at bay  you'll also want a good understanding of  the pros and cons of moon jump  such as normal walking speeds in snow  and sand which is great  but also the drawbacks of bumping into  anything or stepping up a curb  you'll be completely stuck at walking  speeds which is a prime time for a blade  master to one shot you  hold an item in your hands and run if  this happens you'll also need to keep  the camera trained on the blade masters  as they will sometimes despawn and  disappear if you don't  so you'll need to walk with the camera  pointed backwards you'll get used to it  now after a nice long walk and reaching  the korok forest go through the forest  as usual following the wind  it's extra important that you don't mess  up this part as getting lost in the fog  will ruin your run  now that you've reached the master sword  you're not quite done yet the korak  forest and other notable places such as  towns and stables  are considered safe zones where enemies  will usually stray away from  and their ai completely stops to  navigate around this we take advantage  of the blade masters need to confiscate  everything in sight  by dropping a bomb in front of them and  making a breadcrumb trail to the master  sword  once it's close enough to the sword they  spot it and consider it as any other  dropped weapon in need of confiscating  and voila it will approach it and steal  it  [Music]  don't worry though if you reload the  game the sword will be back to normal  which you then can just steal yourself  anyways with another recently found easy  glitch that just yoinks the sword out of  the ground for yourself  the master sword really just can't catch  a break  now you know exactly how this process  works and what you need to do to do it  yourself  if you're curious about other things you  don't know or want more breakdowns  check out our breath of the wild experts  series playlist showing you new and  interesting things  and for everything else gaming stay  tuned right here on gamespot  you
 

